BeatBox — what changed, newest first
=====================================

Packages for each version: https://github.com/lchongv/beatbox/releases


0.99.0, the 1.0 release candidate (7 October 2026)
--------------------------------------------------

What 1.0 will be, to be used for a while first. If nothing turns up, it is
released as 1.0.0 as it is.

- Preferences › Appearance › Edit CSS… edits the skin's CSS with the window
  following as you type and the first error shown with its line. A bundled skin
  is saved as an edited copy in the skins folder.
- New "Template" skin: every color of the Classic look, ready to change. The
  "Native" skin is gone (it looked the same as Adwaita, which it now opens as).
- Podcast episode dates are read in every language (in Spanish, among others,
  they came out wrong).
- With Repeat artist or Repeat album on, playback stopped at the last song of
  the list (or at the first, going back) instead of returning to the start of
  the artist or album.
- Plugins: libbeatbox-core stays compatible for all of 1.x (docs/plugins.md,
  Compatibility). GTK 4 will be 2.0.
- The README shows screenshots, and asks for help with translations.


0.16.1 (6 October 2026)
-----------------------

- Plugins written in Python, besides Vala/C (libpeas-2). The example "Listening
  log" writes a line per song played. The AppImage and the Ubuntu 24.04 package
  can't run them.
- Preferences › Plugins › Install Plugin…; docs/plugins.md explains how to
  write one.
- Plain GTK (Adwaita) is the default look; the previous one is the "Classic"
  skin. New skins: Adwaita dark, Vinyl and High contrast, each with a screenshot
  in Preferences.
- Songs opened from the file manager are the playback list, so Next goes
  through them; a song opened at startup plays once and its play is counted.
- 0.16.0 had no packages: the new smoke test caught the bug above first.


0.15.0 (6 October 2026)
-----------------------

- Plugins, turned on and off in Preferences › Plugins. The first, "Now playing
  file", keeps the playing song in ~/.cache/beatbox/now-playing.txt for
  streaming overlays and status bars.
- Next and Previous follow the list with shuffle on; a song that can't be
  played gapless no longer makes the next one be skipped.
- The library is backed up to ~/.local/share/beatbox/beatbox.db.bak the first
  time a new version opens it.
- Long files on slow disks no longer fail to import.
- iPod sync and audio CD import are marked as experimental.


0.14.0 (6 October 2026)
-----------------------

- An information panel (Ctrl+Shift+I) and a fuller song editor: lyrics,
  pictures, sorting, song identification (AcoustID) and writing every tag to
  the file.
- Long texts in the LCD scroll like a ticker; the time in the LCD is clickable.
- Preferences split into smaller pages.
- Song lists keep their place when they refresh.


0.13.0 (5 October 2026)
-----------------------

- Internet radio in the LCD: a barber pole for the position and the station's
  logo where the cover goes.
- Crisp position markers at large sizes; the app name and version next to the
  window buttons.
- An Arch Linux package.


0.12.0 (5 October 2026)
-----------------------

- A live spectrum in the LCD (the arrow at its left).
- A Nyan cat for the position marker.
- Next and Previous work after opening files.


0.11.0 (5 October 2026)
-----------------------

- .deb (Debian 13, Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04) and .rpm (Fedora) packages.
- No more Granite.


0.10.0 (5 October 2026)
-----------------------

- AppImage and Flatpak packages.
- An editable queue ("Play Next", "Add to Queue", drag to reorder), kept
  between sessions.
- Crossfade between songs, 0–12 s.
- The music folder is watched: new songs are imported, and renamed or moved
  ones keep their play counts and ratings.
- Album art saved into the song files; ListenBrainz scrobbling; configurable
  keyboard shortcuts; a position marker on the time bar.


0.9.0 (4 October 2026)
----------------------

- Volume normalization (ReplayGain) and gapless playback.
- Synced lyrics from LRCLIB on the LCD's second line.
- A mini player (Ctrl+M) and a full-size cover viewer.
- The year is imported from tags again; M4A files keep all their tags.


0.8 (3 October 2026)
--------------------

The original BeatBox, unmaintained since 2013, ported to meson, GTK 3,
GStreamer 1.0, libgee-0.8 and libsoup-3, with a new look, Cover Flow, an
inline cover grid, podcast and radio directories, online album art and skins.
